<title>POLAND: Polish lower house passes 1997 national budget.</title>
<headline>Polish lower house passes 1997 national budget.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's ruling leftist coalition easily pushed through the lower house of parliament the 1997 national budget draft, which envisages maintaining economic growth while cutting inflation.</p>
<p>The house's press office said the draft was approved in a 287 to 123 vote with 14 abstentions. The bill now has to clear the Senate and be signed by President Aleksander Kwasniewski, but neither is expected to oppose it.</p>
</text>
